1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,140
It's hard to believe.

2
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:20,980
Chun-bin is a father.

3
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,020
Feels like he was a rookie just yesterday.

4
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,040
Don't remind me.

5
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,440
He was so impulsive after the academy.

6
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:28,820
Nothing could stop him.

7
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,240
Chun-bin, we're really grateful to you for keeping his head on straight.

8
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:35,540
Well, it's nice of you to say so.

9
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:37,300
But I wasn't much of a mentor.

10
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:39,040
At least not after I quit.

11
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,240
That's in the past.

12
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:42,660
I heard that you're a big-shot lawyer now.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,800
If you ask me, you're better off.

14
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,760
Trust me, you look much better in a suit.

15
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,760
I would have loved for Chun-bin to follow after you,

16
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,600
but that man is police through and through.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,720
That he is, more than I was.

18
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:55,420
Fair.

19
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,120
Now, I'm sure you didn't stop by to see me.

20
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,400
Let me give him a call.

21
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,540
He hasn't been home for a few days.

22
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,960
This case he's on has been running him ragged.

23
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:07,940
Really?

24
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,260
I'd blame his partner.

25
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:14,300
Xiaoli always ends up with the tough cases.

26
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:19,880
Do me a favor.

27
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,460
Answer that for me.

28
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:22,900
Hey, it's me.

29
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:24,760
Are you coming home tonight?

30
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,280
Our daughter has been missing her father,

31
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,800
and Captain Qian stopped by to see you.

32
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:31,580
It's fine.

33
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,340
We're not in a hurry.

34
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:38,940
Promise me you'll get some sleep.

35
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,020
Love you.

36
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:43,560
Well, he's not coming.

37
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,720
Sorry about that.

38
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:46,820
Can't say I'm surprised, though.

39
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,060
He's barely been at home since I got pregnant.

40
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,020
That's the job.

41
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,800
Which is why I went into business for myself.

42
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:58,520
Curious, has he been working on the Chuita Games case recently?

43
00:01:59,220 --> 00:01:59,860
I wouldn't know.

44
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,380
He never tells me anything about his work.

45
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:04,060
And that's fine by me.

46
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,120
I just worry.

47
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:06,640
It's bad for the baby.

48
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:10,120
The first thing I taught him was how to keep his mouth shut.

49
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:13,060
I'm glad to see that at least one lesson's stuck.

50
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:16,300
So, you're having a girl?

51
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:17,540
Maybe.

52
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,060
Nowadays, doctors can't say.

53
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,600
Chun-Bin wants a daughter, though.

54
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,960
So he's been buying stuff like this, despite not knowing.

55
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:27,460
You know what he said?

56
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,480
His faith will change fate.

57
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:30,700
It's that strong.

58
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,260
Can you believe that, man?

59
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,620
He told me the same thing years ago.

60
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:37,800
Oh, right.

61
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,440
I brought you a box of fruit.

62
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,880
Ma, please bring it to the kitchen.

63
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:46,060
Uh, you don't have to carry that heavy thing around.

64
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:47,940
I'll just have Beam do it later.

65
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:48,720
I insist.

66
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,220
Please, sit.

67
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,660
You can put your dirty clothes in this bag after you're done changing, okay?

68
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,380
What's with the stuffed animal?

69
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,220
Not for me, I guess.

70
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:06,340
Uh, I completely forgot about that.

71
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,940
Grabbed it while I was getting your clothes.

72
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,900
It was so cute, I had to buy it.

73
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:13,020
I'm just learning all kinds of things about you today.

74
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,160
It's for my daughter, wise guy.

75
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:18,540
Now go get changed.

76
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:21,700
I'm sorry.

77
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:24,380
I feel bad that you came all this way for nothing.

78
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:25,780
I was in the area.

79
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,480
I'll warn you before showing up next time.

80
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,880
Now go relax.

81
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,160
Get some rest.

82
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,020
I will.

83
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:32,720
Goodbye.

84
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:39,840
I really hope I'm not coming down with a cold.

85
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:43,980
I don't want to be pregnant and sick while my husband can't take care of me.

86
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,920
That was some amazing acting back there, boss.

87
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,700
If I didn't know any better, I'd have thought you were here to see an old friend.

88
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:56,300
Don't you ever burp like that around me again, or I will cut out your throat.

89
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:01,720
Did you get it?

90
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:02,200
Yeah.

91
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:06,540
I snagged one of the ones by the front door when I moved the apples to the kitchen.

92
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:13,580
Sorry I missed you.

93
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:14,880
I'm still busy.

94
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:15,940
Take a rain check?

95
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:16,960
That's fine.

96
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,660
This case must be tricky.

97
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,260
Think you'll be done soon?

98
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,240
Hard to say.

99
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,180
I'm hoping we can wrap this up quick.

100
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,520
I wouldn't want to miss the big day.

101
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:28,200
Yes, that would be a shame.

102
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,360
Fine.

103
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,140
I'll try again sometime.

104
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:32,120
Till then.

105
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,080
Mm-hmm.

106
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:33,560
Thanks.

107
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:33,640
Thanks.

108
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:36,920
All right.

109
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:37,840
How's it fit?

110
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:44,440
Here.

111
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:52,020
It's hard to strangle yourself to death.

112
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,760
Your muscles would give out before you died.

113
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:59,480
We don't know how he did it, but you mean dislocated his cricoid cartilage.

114
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:01,280
Crushed his windpipe.

115
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:02,320
Huh?

116
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,940
If that's true, why did the officer still lie to me?

117
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:08,240
I didn't give you the details because you told me that you already knew.

118
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:09,800
Or I thought you did.

119
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,860
I asked you if you were filled in, remember?

120
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:13,840
How would I know that's what you meant?

121
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,580
Maybe try being a bit more direct next time.

122
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,720
That guy keeping secrets, but that was way too vague.

123
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:20,640
How are you?

124
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:21,040
Huh?

125
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,860
I know everything that happened.

126
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:26,660
I was the one who stabbed Lu Guang.

127
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:34,400
We went over it all, and we have a theory.

128
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:40,260
If this guy does have the power to control people, Liu Min didn't kill himself.

129
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:43,220
He was used in the same way Chao Ling was.

130
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:45,560
There are too many questions.

131
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:47,160
Who is this guy?

132
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,220
Who's he using?

133
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:50,500
How does he do it?

134
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,640
He'll find out that Lu Guang survived.

135
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:54,700
And he'll come for him when he does.

136
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,240
We need to be prepared.

137
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,780
Until we know more, we need any advantage we can get.

138
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,120
This ward is one of them.

139
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,240
Had to get special permission to use it.

140
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:07,600
This building is brand new and hasn't officially been put into use.

141
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:10,880
That means no wandering staff or patients to worry about.

142
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,140
Right now, we're the only ones who know Lu Guang is here.

143
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:16,600
The building also has top-of-the-line surveillance.

144
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:20,100
I made you all accounts on the hospital's network so you can access the feed.

145
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,600
Download the app and stay here.

146
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,280
Keep an eye on things.

147
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:25,840
We'll be on standby.

148
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,620
Anyone shows up, we'll know it's them.

149
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:30,780
Remember, Lu Guang's not here.

150
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,820
Thanks to Chao Ling, you're visiting a family friend.

151
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,200
A family friend?

152
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:36,400
As in...

153
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:38,660
We have no idea who this killer is.

154
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:42,220
I had to find someone we could trust who wasn't very close to us.

155
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:46,180
So I asked Master Suwen if he'd bring his father-in-law in for surgery.

156
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,000
You did what?

157
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,000
Excuse me, he's still recovering.

158
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:50,200
You're the family?

159
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:51,680
Yes, ma'am, we are.

160
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:51,980
Good.

161
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,880
I can go for his post-op care with you.

162
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:55,680
I'm assuming you're both his parents?

163
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:56,980
Not quite.

164
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,240
He's my father, actually.

165
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,300
Wait, white hair but flawless skin?

166
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,140
This man looks young enough to pass for your grandchild.

167
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,860
What is his secret?

168
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,160
This and that.

169
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,300
Doing tai chi, climbing stairs, those kinds of things.

170
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:10,980
That's all?

171
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:13,160
I guess it's true that life is in the movement.

172
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,820
I mean, I would believe it too if I didn't know better.

173
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:21,400
Just shut up.

174
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,500
Thank you both for everything you've done for us.

175
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,940
We appreciate it.

176
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:29,940
This could be nothing, but the killer may have slipped up when we were fighting.

177
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:32,240
It was what he said to me.

178
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:33,640
I can't let it go.

179
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,300
I think his power's like mine.

180
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,200
Wait!

181
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:37,880
No!

182
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:37,980
No!

183
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:45,200
I can't believe it's been right in front of me.

184
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:47,500
You covered that dark room with photos.

185
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,400
Because you need them as well.

186
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,820
It didn't make any sense.

187
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:54,040
Why would he make that connection?

188
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:59,420
No one would assume photos could be used that way, unless they'd done it.

189
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:05,100
If that's the case, then his power most likely relies on photos in the same way that ours do.

190
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:06,560
Or something similar.

191
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,840
That's not all he told me.

192
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,980
Although I don't know how true any of it was.

193
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,940
You're teleporting with pictures?

194
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,400
What a convenient power.

195
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,580
I think I might take it and see what kind of trouble I can get into.

196
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:23,480
As far as I know, our powers can't be taken.

197
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:27,840
But with how confident he was, I'm starting to think that I could be very wrong.

198
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,200
Hey, this ringing any bells for you?

199
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:35,280
I'm not quite sure.

200
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:37,540
That's all I got.

201
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,440
And it's not like I can prove it.

202
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:42,360
But just for safety, I deleted everything we put online.

203
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,780
All our personal stuff, plus anything relating to the photo studio.

204
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:49,600
Which wasn't much, since Liu Guang and I don't post a lot.

205
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:53,680
And he's already a ghost.

206
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,380
He doesn't even have social media.

207
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:57,800
Some might say that he doesn't exist.

208
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:02,680
At least I exist enough to delete those stupid photos you made me take.

209
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:06,580
But I don't post a lot.

210
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,400
How was he able to find something to control me with?

211
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:14,340
When he killed Liu Min, he took the only connection we had to him.

212
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:16,840
This is all we've got now.

213
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,720
Can you check the recent photos?

214
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,580
Chunbin, did you bring the phone like I asked?

215
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,520
Given what we know, we think Liu Min was familiar with the killer.

216
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:29,540
We searched his phone and chat records, but didn't find anything.

217
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,200
It turned out to be a dead end.

218
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:32,800
For us, not you.

219
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,020
Can you find something that we couldn't?

220
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,880
Sure. I'll try.

221
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:42,000
Our IT department was able to crack Liu Min's password.

222
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:46,220
Start with the most recent photos and see what you can learn with that power of yours.

223
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,600
Lu Guang, you're still healing.

224
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,400
Be careful.

225
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,560
Yeah, don't push yourself.

226
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,040
Huh?

227
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,220
Hey, that's Officer Chen's phone.

228
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:05,340
Chenbin?

229
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:06,820
Damn it!

230
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,300
Hang on, I'm coming with you!

231
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:21,400
Actually, it might be better if I stay.

232
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:29,180
Hey, Captain Xiao.

233
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,280
Did you find him?

234
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:31,080
Not yet.

235
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,220
It's like he vanished.

236
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:37,780
Did you notice anything strange when he picked you up?

237
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,680
By the way, I picked you up a change of clothes.

238
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:47,840
So, hey, did they fill you in on the whole situation?

239
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:51,000
Do me a favor, answer that for me.

240
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,720
I might not make it home.

241
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:54,620
I'm still on a case.

242
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,620
Promise you'll get some sleep.

243
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:57,440
Done.

244
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:58,060
Love you.

245
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:04,840
If that's the case, then his power most likely relies on photos in the same way that ours do.

246
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:06,400
Or something similar.

247
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:08,500
Did the killer take control of him?

248
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:16,120
Did Chenbin put this picture away?

249
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:18,880
I guess he wants to use one of the baby.

250
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:24,680
Even if he's being controlled, he should have left to the main exit.

251
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:26,700
I would have seen him by now.

252
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,300
Look how happy your dad is.

253
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:56,140
And soon, he can meet you in person.

254
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,680
Oh, no.

255
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:04,980
Chenbin!

256
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,020
Hey!

257
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:07,940
Hey!

258
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:09,120
Don't you dare!

259
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,060
Come on!

260
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,120
Come on!

261
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:12,920
Tung!

262
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,180
Breathe, damn it!

263
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:15,780
Hey, what's going on?

264
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,340
Captain Xiao, are you still there?

265
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,180
Hello?

266
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,000
Hey!

267
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,500
I've got the surveillance footage on your phone.

268
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,860
Oh, right.

269
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:22,920
Good thinking.

270
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:28,540
No, it's him.

271
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:32,000
But how could Officer Chen fall off the building?

272
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:36,000
I can't love.

273
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:37,640
Someone's coming down from the roof.

274
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:38,620
What?

275
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:42,560
I'll go after him.

276
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,380
The building only has two exits.

277
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,300
Cut him off.

278
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:45,820
Okay.

279
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,740
I'm going with you.

280
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:49,360
No!

281
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,220
Stay here.

282
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,400
Help Lu Guang.

283
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,480
What the hell was that for Xiaoling?

284
00:12:55,480 --> 00:13:02,740
Listen, idiot.

285
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:07,520
I appreciate you trying to protect me, but I don't need it.

286
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:11,020
What I need is your trust!

287
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,660
Get to the first floor.

288
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:18,180
That way, you can cover both exits.

289
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:19,400
What about you?

290
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:20,620
I'll be fine.

291
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,160
I can lock myself in the room.

292
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:27,440
Quit stalling.

293
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,780
Don't let that bastard escape.

294
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,640
I just called it in.

295
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,360
Police are 15 minutes away.

296
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:39,980
Where's Xiaol?

297
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:55,480
We'll have more time to worry about the Captain after we've dealt with the man from the roof.

298
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:57,360
You're right.

299
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,860
You should see an emergency exit.

300
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:02,460
That will give you a straight shot to the first floor so you can cut him off.

301
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:04,380
Yeah.

302
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:07,540
Damn it.

303
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:08,680
Where'd he go?

304
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:11,360
I'm wasting time scrolling through camera feeds.

305
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,140
I need a better picture.

306
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:52,840
Stop right there.

307
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,700
Hey, what are you doing here, Missy?

308
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:00,560
You startled me.

309
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:04,440
Give Lyumian's phone to me.

310
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,740
The police will be here soon.

311
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,100
Just give up.

312
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:26,980
It's all my fault.

313
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,760
Stupid, stupid, stupid.

314
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:32,880
It's all over now, man.

315
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,360
They won't stop until they put a bullet in my head.

316
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,360
What am I going to do?

317
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,300
I don't want to die.

318
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,920
They don't want to die.

319
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:49,600
Wait.

320
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:52,480
First, I'll kill you.

321
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:53,080
Look out.

322
00:15:53,080 --> 00:16:05,800
Never interrupt me.

323
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:21,840
This guy's no joke.

324
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,560
Is he the street fighter Master Seawin talked about?

325
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:25,840
No.

326
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:43,160
Jennifer.

327
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,780
Let's go.

328
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:46,860
Oh.

329
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:48,980
well

330
00:16:48,980 --> 00:17:02,480
.

331
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,320
.

332
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:08,900
.

333
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:13,280
.

334
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:15,360
.

335
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:31,700
You're dead meat, buddy.

336
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:52,640
No way!

337
00:17:52,640 --> 00:18:11,320
That's in time.

338
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:18,760
You find Liu An's phone?

339
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,660
I'm not seeing it.

340
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,520
Officer Chen might still have it.

341
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:25,980
Don't bother!

342
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,700
Her backup's almost here!

343
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,300
Well, that's funny.

344
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:30,940
Mine just arrived.

345
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:56,980
Do what you want with the guy.

346
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:58,720
Leave the girl.

347
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,480
She's all mine now.

348
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:02,640
Hey, talk to me.

349
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:03,660
What's going on?

350
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:04,540
Did you get the phone?

351
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:12,200
No.

352
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:14,200
You

